    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup is anchored today by **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) and **Kyle Tucker** (73.09), our premier plays. **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits immensely from the park factor at play against Suarez, providing a +16% boost that pushes his ceiling into elite territory despite the lefty-lefty matchup. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** draws the most favorable opposing starter in Jackson Kent (5.48 xERA), and despite a projected spot low in the order, his raw talent and the significant skill discrepancy against Kent make him a must-start anchor. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.84) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.26) also provide high-floor stability, both capitalizing on positive platoon dynamics that keep our offensive engine running efficiently.\n\nStrategic optimization highlighted the potential of **Coby Mayo** (65.11), who is elevated into the utility slot today. His exposure to the favorable park conditions and a favorable platoon split against Suarez makes him a superior play over the marginal options on the bench. Conversely, the closest exclusion was **Nasim Nunez** (41.04). While **Nasim Nunez** possesses the sprint speed we prioritize for our SB-starved Roto build, the combination of a tough matchup against Blake Snell and a projected #9 hole in the lineup ultimately suppressed his utility score, keeping him on the bench to preserve our game caps.\n\nCaution is advised regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Kyle Tucker** are all playing under assumed batting orders; should any of these players drop further down the lineup than modeled, their efficiency scores will suffer immediate downward pressure. Additionally, while **Drake Baldwin** (48.10) is slated to start, he faces a difficult assignment in S\u00e1nchez (2.81 xERA). We are relying on his recency and favorable batting position to offset the severe SP skill penalty. Finally, note that **Andy Pages** and **Jacob Wilson** remain unavailable due to injury, limiting our tactical flexibility as we navigate this stretch of the season.",
